  "slug": "fur-squared",
  "name": "FurSquared",
  "shortName": null,
  "description": "FurSquared (F2) is an annual furry convention in the Milwaukee, Wisconsin area, organized by Two Ferrets Co. It was first planned in 2012 at the annual Pride BBQ at Bit Ferret's house in Milwaukee, where guests noted that the barbecue was the closest thing Wisconsin had to a furry convention. The first FurSquared was held February 28 to March 2, 2014. It was held at the Sheraton Hotel in Brookfield through 2023, then moved to the Hilton Milwaukee City Center in 2024 and to the Baird Center area in 2025. Its charity is the Humane Animal Welfare Society of Waukesha, which received a plaque in 2018 thanking the convention for five years of service, and by 2020 the convention had raised over $110,000 for it. Attendance has grown from 555 in 2015 to 2,795 in 2026.",
